<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Entre Ríos</h1><p class="st-meta">1820 CE – 1821 CE · capital Concepción del Uruguay</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived federal republic of the Argentine Littoral, created by the caudillo Francisco Ramírez in 1820.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cepeda-1820">Cepeda</a> in 1820 and signing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pilar">Treaty of Pilar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a> broke with his former leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Artigas</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-league">Federal League</a> and defeated him. In September 1820 he proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province">Entre Ríos</a>, uniting Entre Ríos, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corrientes">Corrientes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/misiones-province">Misiones</a>, with himself as Supreme Chief.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Ramírez</a> organised the republic with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concepcion-del-uruguay">Concepción del Uruguay</a>. He issued regulations on administration, justice and the army, promoted schools and set up a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press. The republic was largely a military creation built around his personal authority and his gaucho cavalry.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1821 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Ramírez</a> launched a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-argentina">Santa Fe</a>. He was defeated and killed in July 1821, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez">Estanislao López</a> displayed his head in Santa Fe. The republic broke up, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province">Entre Ríos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corrientes">Corrientes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/misiones-province">Misiones</a> became separate provinces.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-entre-rios.jpg" alt="Republic of Entre Ríos" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: José Gervasio Artigas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Artigas.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1820 CE – 1821 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Concepción del Uruguay</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Francisco Ramírez</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>República de Entre Ríos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1820&amp;focus=republic-of-entre-rios" aria-label="Republic of Entre Ríos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3185 3358 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Entre Ríos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3505 3614L3517 3686"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3517 3686h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3505 3614h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3505 3614h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Concepción del Uruguay. <a href="/atlas?year=1820&amp;focus=republic-of-entre-rios">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
